From a08040163f84f660ef6bccd75102671733d5af44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:14:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] rdna-boosts: block 06: general system-operations bucket

Campaign fold (wip/moe-expert-cache, beta2): adds the generic backend
expert-cache interface -- `moe_cache_update`, `moe_cache_take_over`,
`moe_cache_promote` and `moe_cache_gather` in the backend iface
(ggml-backend-impl.h) -- so a backend can drive a residency policy for a
host-resident routed-expert table, plus the scheduler half of the consumer:
the routed-expert rebalance onto the layer's owning device and the merged
per-layer MoE split (ggml-backend.cpp), the device-side expert gather that
defers a gatherable routed table from whole-tensor H2D staging, the
input-takeover fast path with its deferred promotion pass, the Meta
delegation to the per-device simple backends (ggml-backend-meta.cpp), and the
`#define GGML_ENV_STR` cache macro the campaign's gates use.  The cache engine
and its CUDA consumers land in block 13; the gemma4 `-sm tensor` exclusion is
in block 14.  The CPU and RPC backend vtables name the four new iface fields
(NULL) so the set stays warning-free.

Amended for the promotion candidate (beta4): keep the scheduler changes prefill-neutral.
The device gather now serves only the below-`sched_stage_min_tokens` band (above it the
r16/r26 whole-shard staging wins: Q4_K_M ub8192 staging 5283 vs gather 4035; `-sm layer`
ncmoe 40 4511 vs 2625), and the routed-expert rebalance is gated to the decode/verify band
(`MUL_MAT_ID` `ne[2] <= 8`), where the cache runs.  Prefill then matches `main` (r28) at
every measured cell while the below-gate gather wins (ub512 +17 %, ub1024 +19 %) are kept.

beta5 (2026-10-02): the device gather now also serves a large (>= 224 MiB) host-resident
expert table above the width gate.  Re-measured with --lazy-mode off (the qwen4exp PLE mmap warm-up
confounds every prefill comparison): qwen4exp 450 MiB ub8192 gather 3052 vs staging 1403; Q8_0
272 MiB 3595 vs 3552; Q4_K_M 144 MiB gather 4291 vs staging 5624, so Q4_K_M keeps the width gate.

r35 (2026-10-04): issue #87's synchronous graph-input fix is now default-on.  The r33
`GGML_SCHED_SYNC_GRAPH_INPUTS=1` A/B candidate still reads the variable, but unset means
enabled; `=0` restores the r26 async behaviour.  The reporter confirmed it clears their
recurrent-state H2D race, and same-seed output is unchanged both ways.

r5 (2026-10-05, PR #96): re-stage a host-resident expert table for a second MUL_MAT_ID
consumer in a later split.  `ggml_backend_sched_split_graph` registered a weight as a split
input only when it first created the copy, so when the same expert weights fed `MUL_MAT_ID`
in two splits the later split reused the earlier split's copy.  With the expert cache armed
that copy was taken over by the 1-row decode-band consumer (`moe_cache_take_over` aliases it
and the op never fills it), so the later wide consumer read stale bytes.  qwen4exp's unmasked
MTP export (a full-row last-layer FFN next to the gathered logits tail) is exactly that second
consumer: the wide op produced NaN in `t_h_nextn`, which reached the drafter's KV and collapsed
MTP draft acceptance across every slot.  When the copy already exists and the node is a
`MUL_MAT_ID` reading WEIGHTS through src[0], register the weights as an input of the current
split as well (once per split), so they are staged for this split's routing.  Single-consumer
graphs are unchanged.  Contributor PR #96 (@briansp2020).
